constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal=Fluid removal:
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.off=§cOff
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.off.desc=Leaves fluids alone, digging and destruction skip them
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.smart=§eSmart
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.smart.desc=Only clears the fluid the removed blocks enclose (up to 64 blocks) and cannot be aimed at; the destruction undo puts the fluid back, the digging undo does not - with fluid storage on, the cleared sources go into the material core and the undo takes them back and restores them
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.on=§aOn
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_removal.on.desc=Fluids are ordinary blocks: they can be aimed at directly (flowing water included); whether flowing and source count as the same kind is decided by the matching mode (similar = same, exact = apart)
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_storage=Fluid storage:
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_storage.no=§cNo
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_storage.no.desc=Cleared fluid simply disappears, nothing is stored
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_storage.yes=§aYes
constructionwandlegacy.option.fluid_storage.yes.desc=Fluid the digging core clears is stored in the material core (in both smart and on mode; needs a bound container that holds fluid, or fluid storage cells in the ME network): one source counts as 1B, flowing fluid as nothing; sources that do not fit stay in the world; undoing consumes the stored fluid and only puts the source blocks back; a source is only dug when it can be stored: a core without fluid storage (no bound container that holds fluid, no fluid cells in the network) or a full store leaves the source in the world
constructionwandlegacy.tooltip.core_removal=§7Shift-click a core button in the wand screen to take that core off
constructionwandlegacy.gui.core_removal_hint=§7Shift-click: take the selected core off
